From d521802c7e94c6e9cb1b8adb7972c2da3663e396 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VCKing101 <59761021+VCKing101@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 21:12:21 +1030
Subject: [PATCH 36/41] GE census: what a game's draws ask of the GE that the
 renderer approximates

<prefix>_GE_CENSUS=<file> checks every draw against a list of features the
renderer does not reproduce exactly and counts the hits per scene, with the
frame and scene each was first seen in and the first draw's state words as
an example, into one JSON file (written at exit, at each scene change and
every 1,800 frames). The list was read off the renderer: state the GE state
machine ignores (logic op, colour test, dither, depth range, depth clamp,
texture map modes, mipmaps and level modes, flat shading, morph weights),
modes the shader approximates (texture functions BLEND and ADD, a texture's
alpha used whatever TCC says, doubled-alpha blend factors, two fixed blend
colours, ABS), primitives not drawn (points, lines), texture cache keys that
miss a change (a CLUT's contents past its first word, CLUT shift, mask and
start, large textures keyed by a sample), render-to-texture read from guest
memory instead of the target (palette or swizzled views, other pixel sizes
or row lengths), targets that change layout or overlap, block transfers and
DMA copies into and out of targets, and draws the renderer dropped.

The input script's new step `scene NAME` starts the next scene. Hooks are
one line each in ge_state.cpp, vulkan_renderer.cpp, main.cpp and
input_script.cpp; with the variable unset each returns at its first test
and nothing changes what is drawn.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
