@@ -82,6 +82,7 @@ Every one of these takes the profile's own prefix, so `TENKAWA_TRACE_KERNEL` for
 | `<PREFIX>_TRACE_SYNC` | Every kernel object a thread waits on, which is how a deadlock is read |
 | `<PREFIX>_TRACE_GE_LIST=N[:M[:W]]` | Every command word of display-list runs N to N+M-1, the first W of each (20000 by default): what a screen that draws nothing is built from |
 | `<PREFIX>_CAPTURE_BLENDED` | A window capture (the input script's `shot`) waits for a present that frame interpolation blended, to look at an in-between frame; with `<PREFIX>_FRAME_RATE_AUTO=0` the rate does not step down while captures stall the frames |
+| `<PREFIX>_GE_CENSUS=<file>` | A JSON census of the GE features the game's draws use that the renderer does not reproduce exactly (ignored state, approximated texture and blend modes, render-to-texture read from guest memory, transfers between targets), counted per scene with the first frame and an example draw's state words; the input script's `scene NAME` starts a new scene (`host/gpu/ge_census.hpp`) |
 | `<PREFIX>_TRACE_SAS` | SAS voices set, keyed on and off, and each change of the end flags a game polls |
 | `<PREFIX>_NO_BUSY_CLOCK` | Keep emulated time still for a thread that never waits, as before the busy clock (`Kernel::charge_busy_time`) |
 | `PSPRECOMP_NO_INTERPRETER=1` | Turn the interpreter off. Nothing runs without a corpus; with one, the runtime stops at the first address the recompiler missed and names it |
